Hi all — adding the implementation checklist and a few pragmatic items from the CS playbook:

- Pre-kickoff: Acme to complete the attached spreadsheet (acme-impl-plan.xlsx) with owners for networking, security, and mobile. Please list the SSO scopes we need — I attached sso-scopes.pdf.

- Dev/dev-test: In your staging, enable verbose logging for token usage for 48–72 hours and exercise the retry paths (simulate 429/503). We can provide a small test token with increased RPS for the test window.

- Client SDK snippet (JS) with full jitter backoff:

const backoff = (attempt) => Math.random() * Math.min(8000, 500 * 2 ** attempt);
async function callGenerate(payload, headers) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    const resp = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(payload), headers });
    if (resp.status === 200) return await resp.json();
    if ([429, 502, 503, 504].includes(resp.status)) {
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff(i)));
      continue;
    }
    throw new Error('Fatal error: ' + resp.status);
  }
  throw new Error('Retries exhausted');
}

- Rate-limit behavior: prefer client-side soft degradation (reduce batch size or fallback to cached responses) rather than aggressive retry. Use Retry-After when present.

